      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{-8}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the number $-8$ is a perfect cube.\n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-8},$ we express $-8$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-2)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-2)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-2)^{3}} & = \\\\ -2 & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
