      "dom_id": "question-44083",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "$\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{64}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that the numbers $125$ and $64$ are both perfect cubes. \n\nSo, to determine the value of $\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{64}},$ we express $\\frac{125}{64}$ as a perfect cube:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{64}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{{5}^{3}}{{4}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5\\cdot 5\\cdot 5}{4\\cdot 4\\cdot 4}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(\\frac{5}{4})}^{3}} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & \\end{aligned}\n$$",
